  "problem": "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $c=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\,4a-(3b-2c).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$4a-(3b-2c)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"2\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"2\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"2\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"2\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
